OUTPUT_QUESTIONS=[]
def output_question(stem,correct,wrong,why,topic='rcode'):
 OUTPUT_QUESTIONS.append({'id':'review-output-'+str(len(OUTPUT_QUESTIONS)+1),'topic':topic,'stem':stem,'options':[correct]+wrong,'correct':0,'why':why})
output_question('The nitric-oxide ANOVA output has Residuals df 19 and Residual Mean Sq 66.8. Which quantity supplies the noise variance for requested follow-up mean comparisons?','66.8',['19','389.7','5.832'],'Residual Mean Sq is the within-group variance estimate; residual df 19 accompanies it.')
output_question('The same ANOVA output has Group df 2, Residual df 19, F 5.832 and p .0106. What does it establish at alpha .05?','At least one population mean differs',['Every pair differs','All means are identical','There is no evidence of a mean difference'],'The overall p is below .05. Which pairs differ requires the requested adjusted follow-up tests.')
output_question('A follow-up to that supplied ANOVA output uses its within variance. Which df should accompany it?','Residual df 19',['New two-group df regardless of the ANOVA','Group df 2 only','The total number of table cells'],'The within variance and its residual degrees of freedom come from the same ANOVA fit.')
output_question('HW2 prints six pairwise chi-square results, but asks only which of three treatments differs from control. How large is the requested family?','Three comparisons',['Six comparisons','One comparison','Four comparisons'],'Use the requested control comparisons, not every printed pair.')
output_question('For those three control comparisons, the chi-square statistics are 18.234, 9.4944 and 4.6895, each with df 1. Which is checked first under Holm?','18.234',['4.6895','9.4944','Their average'],'With the same chi-square df, the largest statistic gives the smallest p and is checked against the strictest level first.')
output_question('A chi-square test output for a two-by-two comparison states Yates continuity correction. Which hand-work recipe matches it?','Subtract .5 from each absolute observed-expected gap, stop at zero, then square',['Subtract .5 after squaring each gap','Ignore the correction for every table','Subtract .5 from the final p value'],'The course requires the half-count correction before squaring for two-by-two tables.')
output_question('A pooled two-sample t result has a negative statistic because group 1 mean is below group 2. How is a two-sided significance decision made?','Compare the magnitude with the two-tail cutoff',['Fail to reject automatically because the statistic is negative','Use only the negative sign','Subtract the sign from the degrees of freedom'],'The sign records direction; both directions can be extreme in a two-sided comparison.')
output_question('The lecture one-sample HR calculation gives t about 2.586 with df 4. The supplied two-tail .05 t cutoff is 2.776. What is the decision?','Fail to reject the reference mean at .05',['Reject because the sample mean is not exactly 72','Reject because t is positive','Conclude the population mean is proved equal to 72'],'The magnitude is below the critical value; the sample does not establish a difference from 72 BPM.')
output_question('For a Normal variable, what does pnorm return when supplied a measurement cutoff, mean and SD?','Cumulative area to the left',['A variance','The inverse cutoff','The density height only'],'The review asks you to understand pnorm and qnorm; pnorm maps a cutoff to cumulative area.')
output_question('What input distinguishes a Normal qnorm calculation from pnorm?','A cumulative probability is supplied to obtain a cutoff',['A sample variance replaces every SD','The function must be a chi-square test','The p value is divided by the sample size'],'qnorm goes from area to location; its spread argument is SD, not variance.')
output_question('The course z comparison uses a critical value from the infinity-df row of the supplied two-tail t table. Why?','The t reference approaches the standard Normal at infinite df',['The number of patients is actually infinite','The test is an uncorrected ANOVA','It makes all probabilities equal to .05'],'The review explicitly points to this row for a two-sided Normal cutoff.')
output_question('A supplied overall categorical test is significant. Before comparing selected group pairs, what must be identified?','The requested pair family and its correction',['A new numerical outcome invented from the category labels','The sum of all printed p values','A random ordering with no pair labels'],'Use the requested pairs, Yates for two-by-two follow-ups, and Bonferroni or Holm to control the overall comparison level.')
